  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Everything is closed except one item, which the policy says must stay open, plus two cancellations I couldn't do myself and you need to make.\n\nOriginal 8 items:\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT abdomen/pelvis 10/19: no cause found for the blood in his urine. The incidental 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is the one already followed in his lung screening. I first ordered the 12-month screening low-dose chest CT (sr-t0001), a tracking task (task-t0002), a patient message and a note. A later addendum changed this (see below).\n- pt-0016 Ondricka, TSH 2.1 (normal): closed. Her potassium was corrected from 6.3 (analyzer error) to 4.4 (normal): closed, no action.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, preliminary CT angiogram of the chest: the final report (dr-00084) shows no clot in the lungs and no nodule (the \"nodule\" was a blood vessel). Closed, no follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, kidney/electrolyte panel (BMP) 10/22: creatinine rose from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 hours, which meets the acute kidney injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP by Monday 10/26 (sr-t0009), urgent patient message, note.\n- pt-0064 Marchetti, creatinine 1.36 on 9/26: no earlier creatinine within 7 days, so not kidney injury. Closed.\n- pt-0033 Whitfield, creatinine 1.31 on 10/22: the 0.84 from 10/21 was entered in error (another patient's sample) and I left it out. Not kidney injury, so closed.\n- pt-0008 Brennan, potassium 6.4 flagged hemolyzed: urgent repeat BMP by Monday (sr-t0015), patient message, note.\n\nResults that arrived while I worked (each handled under §8):\n- pt-0008: the lab withdrew the hemolysis comment, so the 6.4 is real. Switched to the full critical-potassium steps (RBC-LAB-03 §1): stat message to on-call, STAT BMP today (sr-t0019), corrected patient message, RN triage call today (task-t0022), addendum note. His medicines include nothing that commonly raises potassium. I kept metoprolol because stopping a beta-blocker suddenly isn't safe with his heart disease.\n- pt-0033: an urgent care creatinine of 1.78 came in, 9 hours after the 1.31, which meets the kidney injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0026), patient message, note.\n- pt-0064: two new creatinines, 0.88 (10/21) then 1.48 (10/22), which meets the kidney injury rule. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0027), patient message, note. The 9/26 decision stands.\n- pt-0006: the screening program added an addendum to the 4/14 screening CT: a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, rated probably benign, with a repeat scan in 6 months. That scan is due by 11/14, so I ordered the screening CT for 10/23–11/14 (sr-t0034) with a tracking task (task-t0035), sent a corrected patient message and wrote an addendum note.\n\nStill open:\n- pt-0007 Parisian, chest X-ray (inbox-a0002): only a preliminary report exists, showing a possible 7 mm right upper lobe nodule. No final report has been issued, so per §2(c) I left it open. Act on it when the final report comes in.\n- Two orders need cancelling and I have no tool to cancel orders or non-inbox tasks. I created tasks for you to do it:\n  - sr-t0015 (Brennan's Monday BMP, replaced by the STAT order): task-t0024, due today.\n  - sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002 (Patel's April 2027 scan, replaced by the November order): task-t0036.\n\nI didn't touch the 6 refill messages in your messages queue (pt-0027, pt-0030, pt-0031). They came in before I started and aren't part of the results inbox.",
